# Default build-time values for `vite build` (production mode). Real
# secrets never belong here -- this repo's own root .gitignore blocks a
# bare `.env`, but this file is intentionally NOT a secret: it is just the
# fallback Worker origin baked into the static GitHub Pages build when the
# `VITE_API_BASE` CI environment variable (see
# .github/workflows/deploy-pages.yml) isn't set. Left empty here so an
# unconfigured build fails closed (no API origin allowed by the CSP)
# instead of leaking a literal `%VITE_API_BASE%` token into the built
# Content-Security-Policy meta tag. A `VITE_API_BASE` env var set in the
# process environment overrides this at build time.
VITE_API_BASE=
